# DPDPA Compliance Rules

This project processes digital personal data, making it subject to the Indian
Digital Personal Data Protection Act (DPDPA) 2023. When writing or modifying
code that interacts with sensitive data, you must apply the following
guardrails:

## 1. Security Safeguards (Section 8)

- **Plaintext Secrets**: Never hardcode API keys, passwords, database
  connections, or private keys.
- **In-Transit**: Enforce TLS 1.3 across all endpoints. Avoid plain HTTP URLs in
  production config.
- **SSL Verification**: Do not disable SSL validation (`verify=False`,
  `rejectUnauthorized: false`).
- **Cryptography**: Avoid weak algorithms like MD5/SHA1 for hashes involving
  passwords or sensitive data.
- **PII Logging**: Never output plaintext PII (Aadhaar, PAN, phone numbers,
  email, location) in logging systems.
- **PII Encryption**: Store biometrics, Aadhaar, and location telemetry using
  AES-256 field-level encryption.

## 2. Consent & Notice Management (Section 5 & 6)

- **No Pre-Checked Toggles**: Consent checkboxes for cookies, tracking, or
  marketing must be unchecked by default.
- **Consent Gates**: Wrap all third-party analytics/ad pixels (Google Analytics,
  Meta Pixel, Mixpanel, Amplitude) inside consent checks (e.g.
  `if (hasConsent('analytics')) { ... }`).
- **Interoperable Consent Managers**: Expose endpoints/webhooks to handle
  consent revocation requests.

## 3. Storage & Retention Limitation (Section 8(7) & 12)

- **Automated Erasure**: Implement TTL indexes, cron cleanups, or lifecycle
  routines to delete inactive data tables or records (especially location
  histories) within 3 years of last user activity.

## 4. Minor Protection Rules (Section 9)

- **No Behavioral Tracking**: Turn off tracking, targeted ads, and profiling
  logic entirely for accounts flagged as minor users (under 18).
- **Parental Verification**: Enforce parental/guardian consent validation at
  registration for children.

## 5. Data Principal Rights (Sections 11–14)

- **Data Export**: Provide access endpoints ("Download My Data") yielding
  structured user records.
- **Right to Erasure**: Expose cascading deletion pathways to purge accounts and
  child subprocessors.
- **Grievance Channel**: Establish a visible contact (e.g.,
  `privacy@company.com`) and ticketing hook.

## 6. AI/ML Compliance (Module 6)

- **Data Minimization**: Strip out unneeded PII from vector embeddings or model
  feature vectors.
- **Model Security**: Limit public inference APIs with rate limits to prevent
  model extraction.
- **Poisoning Defense**: Sanitize user feedback inputs before routing to
  continuous learning loops.

